      "J-STD-020 sorts non-hermetic surface mount devices into moisture sensitivity levels. The rating says how much ambient exposure a device tolerates before a reflow cycle is likely to damage the package. It says nothing about shelf life, ESD class or solderability.",
      "Read the MSL code from the supplier label, the bag or the device marking, then apply the floor-life rule that J-STD-020 and the label give for that level."
